WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.450
July 1944, a year before the
end of the Second World War.

2
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:08.430
Delegates from 44 countries
meet at Bretton Woods,

3
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:10.390
in the United States.

4
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:14.550
They create the International
Monetary Fund and the World Bank.

5
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:20.890
In 1947, 23 countries sign the General
Agreement on Tariffs and Trade.

6
00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:25.010
Today, the IMF has 191 members.

7
00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.910
Almost every country
is inside this system.

8
00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.170
But do they still favour the
countries that wrote them?

9
00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:34.350
In this mission, you'll trace
how these institutions began,

10
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.070
and what each was set up to do.

11
00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:40.190
Then you'll weigh the evidence on
loans that came with conditions,

12
00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:43.510
and on debt relief for poor countries.

13
00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:48.090
Your mission: decide whether the rules
of the global economy still favour their

14
00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:49.010
founders.
